<title>POLAND: Poland Dec C/A gap $368 mln, $1.35 bln in Jan-Dec.</title>
<headline>Poland Dec C/A gap $368 mln, $1.35 bln in Jan-Dec.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland had a current account deficit of $368 million in December bringing the shortfall in the whole of 1996 to $1.35 billion, the National Bank of Poland said.</p>
<p> POLISH CURRENT ACCOUNT	  DEC  1996    NOV 1996   DEC 1995</p>
<p> current account mln USD	    -368	    -125	  496</p>
<p> merchandise trade balance	  -958	    -805	 -504</p>
<p> exports				 2,447	   2,145	1,989</p>
<p> imports				 3,405	   2,950	2,493</p>
<p> unclassified flows balance	  485	     525	  665</p>
<p>					 JAN-DEC 1996  JAN-DEC 1995</p>
<p> current account mln USD	  -1,352	   5,455</p>
<p> merchandise trade balance	-8,154	  -1,827</p>
<p> exports				24,420	  22,878</p>
<p> imports				32,574	  24,705</p>
<p> unclassified flows balance	7,153	   7,754</p>
<p>Note. From January 1996 the central bank introduced a new category, &quot;unclassified flows&quot; which encompasses mainly cross-border, unregistered trade flows.</p>
<p>The 1995 trade figures were adjusted to make them comparable with 1996 data.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
